  "verbalization": "Cumingianoside E appears to have a shared target relationship with LNCaP through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Cumingianoside E to SNU-387, which in turn targets 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, a compound that ultimately targets LNCaP. The second and third pathways connect Cumingianoside E to Phosphatidylserine synthase 1, which is targeted by Garcinielliptone L and Populoside B, both of which also target LNCaP. These findings suggest that Cumingianoside E may act through a series of downstream targets that ultimately converge on LNCaP, potentially through distinct molecular mechanisms. The evidence supports a complex, multi-tiered interaction where Cumingianoside E influences LNCaP via different intermediaries, highlighting the importance of these intermediaries in the drug's biological activity.",
